#doc (Manual) "Covers and threads together" =>

This section relates the two kinds of structure found so far: the covers at
the bottom of $`F_0` (Section 3) and the dyadic thread $`f` of Section 5.
Apart from its bottom $`f(0) = \bot`, the dyadic thread sits above the first
sixteen rungs; the open interval of every pair of lattice
polynomials in the odd gaps contains countably many threads, pairwise
$`\parallel` (in the vocabulary of Section 2); an element outside the downset
of a table has an upper cover; and the dyadic thread descends to a second cut
that $`F_0` does not fill.  The results are in `wip/f0Structure.lean` and
`wip/f0Hole.lean`.

# The ladder under the thread

Every rung up to $`t_{15}` lies below $`f(d)` for every dyadic $`d > 0`.
PROVED.  The variables of the polynomial $`F_n(m)` are indices $`2^{n} + m \ge 3`,
so $`f(d)` is a lattice polynomial in gaps $`g_k` with $`k \ge 7`; it is true at
the assignment that makes every variable true when $`d > 0`; and
$`t_{15} \vdash t_{2k+1} \vdash g_k` for $`k \ge 7`.

