Each $`e_k` is an order embedding of the dyadic rationals in $`[0, 1]` into the
interval $`[[\![ p ]\!], [\![ q ]\!]]`, with $`e_k(0) \dashv\vdash [\![ p ]\!]` and
$`e_k(1) \dashv\vdash [\![ q ]\!]`, and for $`k \ne k'` the images of the open
interval $`(0, 1)` satisfy $`e_k[(0, 1)] \parallel e_{k'}[(0, 1)]`.  PROVED.  In
the vocabulary of Section 2: for every pair $`p < q` in the lattice generated
by the odd gaps, the open interval $`(p, q)` contains $`\aleph_0` threads,
pairwise $`\parallel`.  (Each image of $`(0, 1)` is a thread through the
order-isomorphism of Section 5 from $`\mathbb{Q}` onto the dyadic rationals in
$`(0, 1)`; that composition is not stated separately in the library.)

